@meta
id: 08-10
title: Rewrite a line, keep the indent
chapter: 08
type: lesson
skills: change-c, substitute-s
par: 116
minutes: 6
vscode: Home, Shift-End, type over the selection
open: order.resolver.ts
vimrc: set autoindent

@brief
Sometimes a line is not worth salvaging. Both resolvers here pull every
order out of the database and filter in memory, which was fine with forty
orders in the seed data and is not fine now.

Rewrite both bodies:

    return this.orderProvider.findOne(id);
    return this.orderProvider.findMany({ customerId });

The indentation is already correct and you should not have to type it.
That is the point of this lesson: the linewise change keeps the indent
and throws away the rest.

@keys
| `cc` | change the whole line — clears it, keeps the indent, inserts |
| `S` | the same command, spelled differently |
| `4j` | four lines down |
| `Esc` | out |

@hints
You met `dd` for "delete this whole line". The change operator doubles the
same way.
--
`cc` empties the line, puts the cursor where the code starts, and leaves
you in insert mode. You type the new body and nothing else.
--
`2j` `cc`, type the first line, `Esc`. Then `4j` `S` and the second one —
`S` and `cc` are the same command.

@solution
    2j cc return this.orderProvider.findOne(id);<Esc>
    4j S  return this.orderProvider.findMany({ customerId });<Esc>  :wq<Enter>

Almost all of that is the new code. The editing part is two keystrokes a
line, and neither line needed selecting, and the indentation looked after
itself.

The indent is worth a word. `cc` keeps it because `autoindent` is on —
this lesson switches it on, and any real vimrc has it. Without it `cc`
clears the line to column zero and you type the spaces yourself. If you
ever find `cc` eating your indentation, that setting is why.

`S` is the same command with another name, and it is the linewise
relative of the `s` you met earlier: `s` substitutes a character, `S`
substitutes a line. Vim has a few of these doubles. Use whichever one
your hand finds; nobody will be able to tell from the file.

@start order.resolver.ts
export class OrderResolver {
  public async order(id: string) {
    return this.orderProvider.findAll().filter((o) => o.id === id);
  }

  public async orders(customerId: string) {
    return this.orderProvider.findAll().filter((o) => o.customerId === customerId);
  }
}

@expected order.resolver.ts
export class OrderResolver {
  public async order(id: string) {
    return this.orderProvider.findOne(id);
  }

  public async orders(customerId: string) {
    return this.orderProvider.findMany({ customerId });
  }
}
